# Build context for ks0man-site.
#
# The Dockerfile COPYs five paths and nothing else, but the whole context is
# still shipped to the builder, so keep it small and - more importantly - keep
# it safe. tools/build_content.py generates the club's FULL content from their
# own private mirror, which contains member names, addresses, phone numbers
# and e-mail addresses. None of that may ever reach a public image, so both
# the generator and anything it writes are excluded from the build context.

.git
.gitignore
.dockerignore
.github

# Anything shaped like a credential. There is no .env in this project - every
# value lives inline in docker-compose.yml - but if someone makes one locally
# it must not ride along into a public image.
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*_rsa
id_*

# Not needed to build or to run the image
*.md
tests
tests/out
docker-compose.yml

# The club's private archive mirror, if it is ever checked out or symlinked
# inside this tree. It holds member names, addresses, phone numbers and
# e-mail addresses. It never enters the build context.
ks0man-migration
mirror
study
**/mirror
**/study

# Four content bundles enter the image: the curated seed; the pages of
# ks0man.com the archive migration did not carry (the roster, the Silent Keys,
# the Field Day galleries); the issues from the years when the newsletter was a
# web page; and the text of the records made from PDF and Word files. All are
# the Society's own record, published in full by its decisions of 17 September
# and 16 October 2026. Anything a build_content.py run produces
# on the club's own machine still stays there.
content/*
!content/seed.json
!content/mirror_pages.json
!content/html_archive.json
!content/record_text.json

# Only the importers run inside the container. build_content.py runs on the
# club's own machine, against their own private mirror, and stays there --
# as does screen_media.py, which also reads it.
#
# This allowlist is load-bearing: tools/import_media.php was added to the
# Dockerfile but not here, so the build context did not contain it and buildx
# failed with `"/tools/import_media.php": not found`. Anything the Dockerfile
# COPYs out of tools/ must be un-ignored here too.
tools/*
!tools/seed.php
!tools/import_media.php
!tools/seed_pages.php
!tools/import_html_archive.php
!tools/lib_tokens.php
!tools/import_record_text.php

# Junk
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
**/.pytest_cache
**/node_modules
**/.DS_Store
**/.idea
**/.vscode
**/*.log
